  "content": {
    "text": "Anthropic has just made its neutered Mythos model fable available to the public, confirming speculation that the product would launch today.\nKey Highlights: Claude Fable 5 & Claude Mythos 5 Launch\n-\nClaude Fable 5 released publicly as a Mythos-class model with advanced safety guardrails.\n-\nClaude Mythos 5 offers the same core model with fewer restrictions for approved researchers.\n-\nState-of-the-art performance across coding, reasoning, vision, scientific research, and long-context tasks.\n-\nCybersecurity and bio-risk safeguards automatically route sensitive queries to Claude Opus 4.8.\n-\nPricing set at $10 input / $50 output per million tokens, less than half Mythos Preview.\nBiggest Claims\n-\nStripe said Fable 5 compressed months of engineering work into days.\n-\nFable 5 completed a large Ruby codebase migration that would have taken a team over two months.\n-\nMythos 5 reportedly achieved 10× acceleration in parts of the drug-design process.\n-\nAnthropic says Mythos 5 generates novel scientific hypotheses preferred by researchers ~80% of the time.\n-\nThe model conducted week-long autonomous genomics research, outperforming a recent published model despite being 100× smaller.\nSafety & Access\n-\nSensitive cybersecurity, biology, chemistry, and model-distillation requests trigger fallback to Claude Opus 4.8.\n-\nAnthropic says safeguards activate in less than 5% of sessions.\n-\nMythos 5 is currently limited to Project Glasswing partners and selected biology researchers.\n-\nBusiness users of Mythos-class models will face mandatory 30-day data retention for safety monitoring.\nAvailability\n-\nFable 5 is available immediately.\n-\nIncluded on Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise plans until June 22, 2026.\n-\nAfter June 23, usage credits may be required until capacity expands.\nAnthropic is effectively introducing a new AI tier above Opus, claiming frontier-level gains in coding, scientific research, cybersecurity, and autonomous work—while using extensive safeguards to enable broader public access.\nThe following section was published earlier after reports hinted at an imminent Claude Mythos launch later today, June 9, 2026.\nAnthropic is expected to release the public version of its powerful Mythos AI model today, June 9, 2026, under the name Claude Fable, according to a report on The Information.\nThe move brings advanced cybersecurity capabilities into broader access, delivering both opportunities and urgent risks for the cryptocurrency sector.\nAnthropic's Mythos Arrives Amid High Expectations\nAnthropic first introduced Claude Mythos Preview in April 2026 through Project Glasswing, a restricted program involving partners like AWS, Microsoft, Apple, and CrowdStrike.",
